prompt:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: production scenery sprite atlas for an interactive Vietnamese xianxia RPG quest journal.
Primary request: ONE perfectly aligned landscape 3:2 image with EXACTLY THREE equal columns and TWO equal rows, SIX independent SQUARE scenery paintings. Every cell fills its allotted square, no gutters, no frames, no overlaid icons or words. Hand painted high-end Chinese immortal fantasy game illustration matching ornate navy/gold RPG UI; rich but readable at thumbnail size.
Order left to right, top to bottom:
1. humble peaceful ancient Chinese riverside village at early morning, tiled roofs, willow tree, round village well, warm lanterns and small wooden bridge;
2. majestic immortal sect mountain courtyard at moonlight, glowing lanterns, blue roof temple gates and pink peach blossoms, navy-blue atmosphere;
3. enchanted emerald herb forest, luminous medicinal leaves in foreground, turquoise stream and tall ancient trees;
4. dangerous icy-blue crystal cavern and ancient sealed gate, distant small silhouette of a ferocious guardian beast, dramatic deep blues;
5. warm golden alchemy chamber with bronze incense cauldron, shelves with herbs and ceramic bottles, gentle gold fire glow;
6. stone sword training courtyard with circular carved floor and small wooden training dummy, temple roofs behind, blue mountain mist, warm lanterns.
All six cells are consistent detailed painterly game scenes, strong compositions, each self-contained and safely inside its own square, with distinct color moods.
Constraints: no text, no lettering, no digits, no writing on banners, no labels, no UI, no panel borders, no characters in foreground, no watermark.
